WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:12.400
Hello, my name is Pyo Ye-Rim...

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:19.600
By the time you see this video,
I will be about to end my life...

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:24.160
unless I already have.

00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:32.080
She had spoken out on social media

00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:38.880
about the bullying she suffered
at school when she was young..

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:43.200
The police are investigating
the e circumstances of her death.

00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:47.200
She announced her intention
to end her life in a video online.

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:51.120
She said that she was really struggling
with the criticism aimed at her

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:53.520
after she had spoken out against bullying.

00:00:53.800 --> 00:00:56.960
Pyo Ye Rim died by suicide on October 10,

00:00:57.240 --> 00:00:59.040
2023.

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:00.760
She was 27 years old.

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:02.520
She had become a whistleblower,

00:01:02.680 --> 00:01:05.760
an activist speaking out against violence in schools.

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:09.280
Violins,

00:01:09.800 --> 00:01:12.240
which she herself endured for 12 years.

00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:20.200
She grew up in this coastal region in the southeast of the country.

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:23.160
where she was bullied year after year,

00:01:23.800 --> 00:01:26.240
all the way up to the end of secondary school.

00:01:26.240 --> 00:01:33.040
What she went through could happen to anyone.

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:39.360
Anyone could have been traumatised like
she was, and suffered the consequences.

00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:52.160
My name is Kim Hyo-Kyung.
I'm 28 years old.

00:01:52.320 --> 00:02:00.160
I spent a year at the same girls' school as Ye-Rim.

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:08.240
As soon as she went to class,
the other pupils bullied her.

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:12.400
They hit her.

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:20.480
They would storm into the classroom, shouting
and insulting her. They kicked her desk.

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:28.400
They dragged her to the toilet
and plunged her head into the bowl.

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:32.800
I can only imagine how badly
she wanted to get away.

00:02:34.640 --> 00:02:38.120
Pyongye Rim was the first to go public with her story.

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:45.000
We met her a few weeks before her death to bring attention to her cause.

00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:51.000
Her contribution was central to our film on bullying in South Korea.

00:02:52.400 --> 00:03:00.160
I have often wondered whether
I should go on living through all this.

00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:05.120
Whether I have to die for it to stop.

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:13.200
One day, at secondary school or high school, I don't
know which, a girl came in the middle of class.

00:03:13.360 --> 00:03:18.320
She came in and told me to follow her.

00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:24.400
I left without suspecting anything.

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:31.760
She beat me up for 10 minutes, without mercy.

00:03:31.920 --> 00:03:34.880
And all this while the teacher was in class.

00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:39.760
He told me I was the one who wasn't
making an effort to get on with the others.

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:43.600
He said, 'Are you sure you
haven't done anything to them?"

00:03:46.680 --> 00:03:49.640
She didn’t go to college after the second degree of school

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:53.640
She was to affraid of running to the people who had bullied her

00:03:54.120 --> 00:03:58.040
She opened a hairdressing salon and tried to rebuild her life.

00:03:58.720 --> 00:04:01.680
We started filming with her here at the salon.

00:04:02.280 --> 00:04:02.960
At the time,

00:04:03.280 --> 00:04:05.640
no one suspected what she was going through,

00:04:06.040 --> 00:04:07.200
not even her parents.

00:04:07.560 --> 00:04:08.320
Ten years later,

00:04:08.800 --> 00:04:11.760
she decided to tell her story to the whole country.

00:04:12.360 --> 00:04:15.240
Thousands of young Koreans identified with her.

00:04:21.280 --> 00:04:29.280
An 11-year-old primary school pupil
died by suicide yesterday morning.

00:04:29.440 --> 00:04:34.720
A primary school pupil took his own life
"because of bullying at school".

00:04:36.280 --> 00:04:38.760
Korea has the highest suicide rate in the world.

00:04:39.360 --> 00:04:42.240
There are more than 30 recorded cases every day.

00:04:43.080 --> 00:04:45.320
And suicides often lead the news.

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:51.160
The rate is especially high among young people and among those who are bullied at school.

00:04:51.680 --> 00:04:51.840
With

00:04:52.200 --> 00:04:54.720
60,000 cases reported each year,

00:04:55.600 --> 00:04:56.000
films,

00:04:56.360 --> 00:05:01.640
books and TV series all show this national crisis in their storylines.

00:05:02.280 --> 00:05:08.480
One of the latest hit series tells the story of a model pupil who ends up standing up to his attackers.

00:05:10.240 --> 00:05:13.040
This is exactly what Pyo Ye Rim dared to do.

00:05:13.520 --> 00:05:17.200
When she spoke out on social media about what had happened to her,

00:05:17.680 --> 00:05:19.000
she received some support,

00:05:19.240 --> 00:05:21.080
but also thousands of attacks.

00:05:21.360 --> 00:05:23.240
It was a wave of cyberbullying.

00:05:23.560 --> 00:05:25.040
She had not anticipated the...

00:05:25.160 --> 00:05:29.800
violence and scale of it the issue of school violence long a taboo subject

00:05:29.800 --> 00:05:36.800
 has inflamed public opinion journalist Lee Ye Wong was the last person to speak with Pyo Ye Rim 

00:05:36.800 --> 00:05:41.880
she believes that Pyo Ye Rim made it possible for other people to speak out

00:05:42.320 --> 00:05:47.360
You could say that she died
for her cause, like a martyr.

00:05:47.760 --> 00:05:52.560
Not many victims of bullying reveal
their identity to the general public,

00:05:52.720 --> 00:05:57.360
so I think that's why she had such an influence.

00:05:57.600 --> 00:06:03.120
In recent years, more and more voices
have spoken out to say that this had to stop,

00:06:03.280 --> 00:06:06.720
that the scourge of school violence had to end.

00:06:06.880 --> 00:06:14.800
Pyo Ye-Rim embodied this turning point
in society by denouncing the system.

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:23.040
Whenever she had free time,
she studied the laws on bullying at school.

00:06:23.200 --> 00:06:29.200
She was very committed to her fight.

00:06:31.080 --> 00:06:34.200
She set up an organization to help other victims.

00:06:34.920 --> 00:06:36.400
A few months before her death,

00:06:36.800 --> 00:06:40.640
she launched a petition to hold bullies to account for their actions.

00:06:50.480 --> 00:06:51.160
This lawyer,

00:06:51.600 --> 00:06:52.680
John Ho Sung,

00:06:53.160 --> 00:06:56.160
helped her to collect more than 50,000 signatures.

00:06:58.120 --> 00:07:05.200
Together they worked on a bill to revise the statute of limitations in cases of violence in schools.

00:07:10.640 --> 00:07:14.080
Pyo Ye Rim was never able to bring her bullies to justice.

00:07:14.880 --> 00:07:18.760
They are now adults and the statute of limitations has expired.

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:23.240
This is precisely the change that she wanted to make.

00:07:24.200 --> 00:07:28.880
They worked with this MP on their proposal which is due to be submitted to parliament.

00:07:29.280 --> 00:07:36.160
She was surprised by the
number of signatures collected.

00:07:36.320 --> 00:07:41.600
I tried very hard to comfort Pyo.

00:07:41.760 --> 00:07:45.840
I told her that you would be
the one who could help us.

00:07:46.000 --> 00:07:53.920
I explained that with your support, you would
get this law passed as quickly as possible.

00:07:54.080 --> 00:08:01.200
Obviously, I still have to work to ensure
that the bill has every chance of being passed.

00:08:01.360 --> 00:08:06.480
The petition you've launched will
be a great help, that's for sure.

00:08:06.720 --> 00:08:12.800
And will enable us to go
even further in our requests.

00:08:13.280 --> 00:08:18.400
We need to change our penal code and the law.

00:08:18.560 --> 00:08:22.320
Victims, even years after the event,
must be able to lodge a complaint.

00:08:22.480 --> 00:08:28.640
They must be able to defend
themselves and obtain compensation.

00:08:28.800 --> 00:08:32.240
This is the only way to protect our young people.

00:08:32.400 --> 00:08:37.200
Minors must be able to take action
once they have become adults.

00:08:51.520 --> 00:08:59.440
I know a lot of people who have been
through what Pyo Ye-Rim went through.

00:09:00.320 --> 00:09:07.760
But she is one of the rare people
to have spoken out publicly on this issue.

00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:17.520
Today, bullying at school is
a real issue in Korean society.

00:09:17.680 --> 00:09:23.120
Any high-ranking official, celebrity
or public figure who is involved, or even sees

00:09:23.280 --> 00:09:29.680
his or her children directly or indirectly involved
in a case of bullying, has questions to answer...

00:09:29.840 --> 00:09:32.960
This subject is getting a lot of attention today.

00:09:33.120 --> 00:09:38.080
But at the time when Pyo Ye-Rim was going
through all this, it wasn't yet the case.

00:09:45.400 --> 00:09:46.640
It's an important issue,

00:09:47.080 --> 00:09:53.280
so much so that a hashtag was created in 2023.

00:09:53.280 --> 00:09:54.120
Call out your bully.

00:09:54.680 --> 00:09:55.920
It was like Me Too,

00:09:56.360 --> 00:09:57.720
but for violence in school.

00:09:58.520 --> 00:10:02.160
Tens of thousands of stories flooded social media platforms.

00:10:02.880 --> 00:10:06.160
People denounced their bullies publicly years later.

00:10:07.320 --> 00:10:13.680
There was such an unprecedented wave of accusations that it sometimes started to look like a witch hunt.

00:10:14.680 --> 00:10:16.840
Not even celebrities have been spared.

00:10:17.880 --> 00:10:18.240
Singers,

00:10:18.520 --> 00:10:19.600
sportsmen and women,

00:10:20.160 --> 00:10:20.600
actors,

00:10:20.880 --> 00:10:21.560
actresses,

00:10:22.080 --> 00:10:23.360
senior civil servants.

00:10:24.160 --> 00:10:27.960
Anyone involved in bullying in any way could be ostracized,

00:10:28.280 --> 00:10:30.840
lose their job or be forced to resign.

00:10:32.160 --> 00:10:33.240
There is a lot of talk,

00:10:33.720 --> 00:10:35.600
but no action to address the problem.

00:10:43.880 --> 00:10:44.920
Two hours from Seoul,

00:10:45.320 --> 00:10:46.480
there is a unique school.

00:10:47.360 --> 00:10:53.680
It's a boarding school for children and teenagers who have been victims of bullying and have developed school phobia.

00:10:54.640 --> 00:10:56.640
Even if their bullies have been reported,

00:10:57.200 --> 00:11:00.680
they're too scared of reprisals once they are back in class.

00:11:06.160 --> 00:11:13.760
Today we're welcoming a new pupil.
He's a very nice boy.

00:11:13.920 --> 00:11:21.280
I'm relying on you to make him feel welcome.

00:11:24.280 --> 00:11:25.360
In this boarding school,

00:11:25.760 --> 00:11:31.080
around 50 teenagers receive a traditional education alongside counselling.

00:11:32.600 --> 00:11:33.960
Is the water here the sea or...?

00:11:34.320 --> 00:11:40.120
The children live here in a safe space and stay as long as it takes before they can go back to school.

00:11:40.880 --> 00:11:43.840
It might be a few weeks or even several months.

00:11:47.640 --> 00:11:50.640
16-year-old Min Sam Mool arrived a week ago.

00:11:54.800 --> 00:12:00.160
I had nowhere to go, I was completely lost.

00:12:00.320 --> 00:12:05.040
But I couldn't give up my
studies either, so I came here.

00:12:05.200 --> 00:12:11.680
If you ask any of us to go back
to school, none of us want to go.

00:12:11.840 --> 00:12:18.960
We're all the same, even those with more money.

00:12:19.280 --> 00:12:23.280
It's our last option because we've reached our limit.

00:12:25.080 --> 00:12:25.680
The centre,

00:12:25.720 --> 00:12:27.960
which has seven other regional branches,

00:12:28.280 --> 00:12:29.160
is entirely private.

00:12:29.200 --> 00:12:30.160
privately funded.

00:12:30.920 --> 00:12:36.400
There are no other facilities of this type in Korea apart from psychiatric hospitals.

00:12:41.040 --> 00:12:42.000
For many parents,

00:12:42.080 --> 00:12:43.800
like Min Sam-mool's parents,

00:12:44.280 --> 00:12:45.640
this is a last resort.

00:12:49.520 --> 00:12:52.160
I had a lot of questions...

00:12:52.320 --> 00:12:55.760
I wanted to listen to someone who had
been through the same experience

00:12:55.920 --> 00:12:59.600
to find out how to help my child feel better.

00:12:59.840 --> 00:13:03.120
That's the kind of help I came here for.

00:13:03.280 --> 00:13:11.200
Before, we were completely lost,
even when we were at home.

00:13:11.360 --> 00:13:17.920
It was affecting my work.

00:13:18.080 --> 00:13:25.760
For us, this centre not only cares for
young people, but also for us parents.

00:13:27.440 --> 00:13:32.080
I saw my child's confidence
plummet when he was bullied.

00:13:32.560 --> 00:13:36.560
Right up to the point where he
talked about taking his own life.

00:13:36.720 --> 00:13:41.440
Obviously, as parents, we have a
lot of expectations of our children.

00:13:41.600 --> 00:13:44.000
I always wanted mine to do better than me.

00:13:44.160 --> 00:13:48.160
That's why I asked a lot of him,
demanding that he get over this quickly.

00:13:48.320 --> 00:13:50.800
But he never really regained his self-confidence.

00:13:50.960 --> 00:13:55.120
During that time, he actually
attempted suicide, which I witnessed.

00:13:55.280 --> 00:13:57.680
Since then, I've radically changed my opinion.

00:13:57.840 --> 00:14:04.000
It doesn't matter whether he studies well or not,
all that matters is that he's alive beside me...

00:14:04.160 --> 00:14:07.280
And that he has a long life.

00:14:09.640 --> 00:14:11.840
These parents are often at a loss.

00:14:12.440 --> 00:14:15.000
They're powerless in the face of their children's bullies,

00:14:15.480 --> 00:14:17.720
who can even sue for defamation.

00:14:18.960 --> 00:14:19.600
This actually happened to me.

00:14:28.400 --> 00:14:34.400
When we accused the culprits,
they accused us of defamation.

00:14:34.560 --> 00:14:36.400
And how did that make you feel?

00:14:36.560 --> 00:14:42.720
Well, I was taking a walk when I saw
a letter from lawyers, and I fainted twice.

00:14:42.880 --> 00:14:48.000
My head was spinning, and my legs
couldn't carry me. I really did fall twice.

00:14:48.160 --> 00:14:50.720
And I couldn't sleep at night. It was so difficult.

00:14:50.880 --> 00:14:55.360
The hardest thing is accepting
that a lawyer has decided

00:14:55.520 --> 00:14:57.920
to help guilty people get away with what they did.

00:14:58.080 --> 00:15:03.440
All they did was lie and accuse my daughter of
being responsible for the cruelty she suffered.

00:15:03.600 --> 00:15:06.240
We are the ones who have suffered because of them.

00:15:06.400 --> 00:15:10.560
Not only did they refuse to apologise,
but they also attacked us.

00:15:10.720 --> 00:15:12.880
For us, it was like rubbing salt in the wound.

00:15:15.280 --> 00:15:17.000
Rather than acknowledge the facts,

00:15:17.400 --> 00:15:19.000
the bullies counterattack.

00:15:19.960 --> 00:15:25.480
Bullies will sue for defamation to avoid the serious consequences of being held accountable.

00:15:26.240 --> 00:15:27.400
In 2026,

00:15:27.760 --> 00:15:30.000
a national database will be set up,

00:15:30.520 --> 00:15:35.080
and all those found guilty of bullying will be banned from the best universities.

00:15:35.840 --> 00:15:39.000
So they deny it and call the victims liars,

00:15:39.520 --> 00:15:41.320
insult them and threaten them.

00:15:47.280 --> 00:15:54.960
There are two ways of overcoming fear.
Either you try to put it aside...

00:15:55.120 --> 00:15:59.200
or you give way to anger..

00:15:59.600 --> 00:16:01.920
I'm angry.

00:16:02.080 --> 00:16:05.840
And that anger will make me a strong woman.

00:16:06.000 --> 00:16:08.960
Don't try and stop me.

00:16:09.120 --> 00:16:14.960
Don't think I'm making this video
to get back at you or to scare anyone.

00:16:15.200 --> 00:16:21.520
I'm making it for the students
who are being bullied right now,

00:16:21.680 --> 00:16:27.520
and against those who are committing
crimes at this very moment.

00:16:30.280 --> 00:16:34.280
Lee Se-wook was the first to share Pyongye Rim's story online.

00:16:34.760 --> 00:16:37.120
He's what's known in Korea as a netizen,

00:16:37.800 --> 00:16:39.120
an internet vigilante,

00:16:39.560 --> 00:16:41.000
and whistleblower.

00:16:41.920 --> 00:16:47.920
I was the one who contacted the national channels

00:16:48.080 --> 00:16:55.760
Her story made the headlines
and changed public opinion.

00:16:55.920 --> 00:17:03.600
Immediately, a girl who probably
went to the same school

00:17:03.760 --> 00:17:10.800
as Pyo Ye-Rim showed all the faces
and names of the alleged culprits.

00:17:10.960 --> 00:17:18.560
Everything moved very fast on social media.

00:17:18.560 --> 00:17:20.160
12

00:17:20.480 --> 00:17:27.200
People became interested in her attackers.

00:17:27.360 --> 00:17:33.600
Some of them lost their jobs or had to resign
in the face of the avalanche of criticism.

00:17:33.760 --> 00:17:37.520
Pyo Ye-Rim was pleased.

00:17:38.080 --> 00:17:45.920
She said that she was lucky to have won
people's hearts, which had made it possible

00:17:46.080 --> 00:17:51.520
to finally pinpoint the culprits.

00:17:51.680 --> 00:17:56.960
But she didn't want to stop there.

00:18:07.760 --> 00:18:08.080
Education in Korea is very much
marked by the legacy

00:18:08.080 --> 00:18:08.360
here again,

00:18:08.360 --> 00:18:15.440
Education in Korea is very much
marked by the legacy

00:18:15.600 --> 00:18:22.160
of the Japanese occupation that we experienced.

00:18:22.320 --> 00:18:30.160
It's a military system where the interests of
the group take precedence over the individual.

00:18:30.320 --> 00:18:38.080
If a single person endangers the group, even
slightly, they end up being completely rejected.

00:18:38.240 --> 00:18:46.160
I think it's a culture that's
very deeply rooted in our society.

00:18:46.320 --> 00:18:54.000
It permeates the Korean education
system and has never disappeared.

00:18:54.160 --> 00:19:00.720
When a student is abused or left out,

00:19:00.880 --> 00:19:07.360
they are rejected to protect the majority.

00:19:08.600 --> 00:19:15.400
Pyo Ye-rim underestimated the outpouring of hatred on social media that would follow her revelations.

00:19:16.000 --> 00:19:17.600
Her bullies resurfaced.

00:19:20.640 --> 00:19:24.480
It must have surprised them.

00:19:25.680 --> 00:19:28.400
They had forgotten everything.

00:19:28.560 --> 00:19:34.000
The bullies must have thought,
"Why is she bringing this up again?"

00:19:35.200 --> 00:19:39.600
They ended up killing Ye-Rim.

00:19:40.560 --> 00:19:45.040
Just as much as she killed herself.

00:19:45.200 --> 00:19:52.560
Many more people drove her
to suicide than you might think.

00:19:54.000 --> 00:20:01.520
When she told her story of bullying,
many people sided with the guilty.

00:20:01.680 --> 00:20:08.320
Some criticised her for only
speaking out now and said

00:20:08.480 --> 00:20:13.760
that she hadn't really suffered
12 years of harassment.

00:20:13.920 --> 00:20:18.800
Her bullies were not the only
ones responsible for her death.

00:20:18.960 --> 00:20:22.160
A very large number of people are.

00:20:24.800 --> 00:20:26.600
The school system is another factor,

00:20:27.320 --> 00:20:29.480
as it often pushes pupils to their limit.

00:20:30.080 --> 00:20:31.520
Every evening in the capital,

00:20:31.640 --> 00:20:31.920
Seoul,

00:20:32.480 --> 00:20:35.200
busloads of students are taken to the hagyons,

00:20:35.680 --> 00:20:40.400
private after-school academies where they will do another full day of classes.

00:20:41.200 --> 00:20:44.120
That's what it takes to pass the university entrance exam.

00:20:45.360 --> 00:20:48.120
Many of them study for up to 20 hours a day.

00:20:49.160 --> 00:20:51.080
It's a highly competitive environment,

00:20:51.400 --> 00:20:54.120
and parents share this obsession with success.

00:20:57.520 --> 00:21:03.120
This academy pushes you
to study harder than any other.

00:21:03.280 --> 00:21:10.000
If you study for fifteen hours a day, for example,
you have three hours to eat and six hours to sleep.

00:21:10.240 --> 00:21:16.240
All they do is study, sleep and eat.

00:21:18.520 --> 00:21:21.240
Parents spend little time with their children,

00:21:21.880 --> 00:21:26.440
and they expect teachers to focus on imparting as much knowledge as possible.

00:21:27.640 --> 00:21:31.680
This parallel system of private schools has become the norm in Korea.

00:21:32.640 --> 00:21:35.920
The government has even tried to regulate them by imposing a

00:21:36.320 --> 00:21:37.600
10pm closing time.

00:21:37.760 --> 00:21:43.040
I think it's hard to change the
system because, at the end of the day,

00:21:43.200 --> 00:21:46.400
competition is the mainstay of private education.

00:21:46.560 --> 00:21:54.160
At the end of the day, if you want to get into the
university of your dreams and get the job you want,

00:21:54.320 --> 00:21:59.600
you have to accept this competitive system.

00:22:02.280 --> 00:22:04.640
But with all of this pressure on achievement,

00:22:05.080 --> 00:22:07.320
no one seems to be focusing on the students'

00:22:07.360 --> 00:22:09.040
problems with socialization.

00:22:10.040 --> 00:22:13.480
The pressure might be one of the factors behind violence in schools.

00:22:14.240 --> 00:22:17.560
Pyongyang Rim revealed the hidden face of the school system.

00:22:18.440 --> 00:22:24.200
Education had a positive image in Korea based on the entire nation's academic success.

00:22:24.920 --> 00:22:27.640
It was held up as being the gold standard.

00:22:28.240 --> 00:22:31.560
But vulnerable pupils were left to cope without support.

00:22:32.040 --> 00:22:34.560
Other citizens now want to challenge this system.

00:22:34.880 --> 00:22:35.920
Like Kim Jong-ki,

00:22:36.400 --> 00:22:41.240
he knew Pyongyang Rim well and knew about her campaign and her commitment.

00:22:42.160 --> 00:22:43.640
They were supposed to work together,

00:22:44.360 --> 00:22:46.640
but that was before she took her own life.

00:22:47.040 --> 00:22:48.040
He didn't see it coming,

00:22:48.320 --> 00:22:50.800
just as he didn't see it coming when his own

00:22:51.320 --> 00:22:53.560
13-year-old lost his life to suicide.

00:22:56.160 --> 00:23:03.600
I felt a pain that no other parent
should feel in their life.

00:23:03.760 --> 00:23:10.800
It was like the sky fell on me,
and everything descended into chaos.

00:23:11.760 --> 00:23:18.080
I find it very difficult to express
my pain in front of others.

00:23:18.240 --> 00:23:25.120
I prefer to stay alone to think, talk and pray.

00:23:26.880 --> 00:23:34.800
I see myself as a bad father who didn't
pay attention to his son's suffering.

00:23:36.320 --> 00:23:43.280
I was too focused on my work
to help with his problems.

00:23:43.440 --> 00:23:48.800
I feel very ashamed.

00:23:48.960 --> 00:23:54.960
I've lost all will to live.

00:23:55.120 --> 00:24:02.000
Why live when I couldn't protect him?

00:24:02.160 --> 00:24:09.520
What's the point of being a company boss
and making millions?

00:24:16.200 --> 00:24:23.040
His son Kim Dae-hyun died by suicide after jumping out of the window of the family's fifth floor flat.

00:24:23.920 --> 00:24:27.640
He had never mentioned his suffering from being regularly bullied.

00:24:30.160 --> 00:24:35.840
He never looked happy.

00:24:36.000 --> 00:24:43.760
For a while before he died, he would come back
with wounds, bruises, broken glasses.

00:24:43.920 --> 00:24:51.200
It happened almost every day.

00:24:51.360 --> 00:24:56.160
I met his attackers in a bakery.

00:24:56.320 --> 00:25:00.640
I asked each of them why they had hurt my son.

00:25:00.800 --> 00:25:04.240
They were trembling with fear.

00:25:04.400 --> 00:25:10.400
They stuttered and kept apologising.
Their attitude destroyed me.

00:25:10.560 --> 00:25:17.760
I wanted to kill them. Well, not with
my own hands, I couldn't do that.

00:25:17.920 --> 00:25:24.160
I planned to hire an organisation
to kill them in Korea,

00:25:24.320 --> 00:25:27.760
before leaving the country to settle
in South America or Africa.

00:25:27.920 --> 00:25:29.920
That was my plan.

00:25:30.080 --> 00:25:35.360
I was ready to do it, but when I saw them
trembling in front of me, I felt sorry for them.

00:25:35.520 --> 00:25:38.160
I don't know if you can understand.

00:25:41.960 --> 00:25:45.080
This tragedy shook Kim Jong-ki very deeply.

00:25:45.880 --> 00:25:49.600
He was wracked with guilt for not having been able to protect his son.

00:25:50.520 --> 00:25:54.480
So he set up his own foundation to help victims and their parents.

00:25:55.280 --> 00:25:56.840
He regularly appeals to the public.

00:25:56.840 --> 00:25:57.720
public authorities.

00:25:58.240 --> 00:26:02.000
And he feels that they still don't fully appreciate the scale of the problem.

00:26:02.400 --> 00:26:04.080
The consequences are devastating.

00:26:04.680 --> 00:26:07.920
Hundreds more families suffer bereavement every year.

00:26:08.440 --> 00:26:11.760
Kim Jong-ki's foundation now has 14 branches.

00:26:12.000 --> 00:26:13.200
throughout South Korea,

00:26:14.000 --> 00:26:17.280
with 300 employees and as many volunteers.

00:26:18.240 --> 00:26:25.120
It has set up counselling and psychological support units with telephone help lines for parents and pupils.

00:26:26.000 --> 00:26:30.640
And what did you try to do?

00:26:31.680 --> 00:26:35.600
The school said they were going to separate them,

00:26:35.760 --> 00:26:41.920
but my child has only been able to go
to school one day in the last nine months.

00:26:42.160 --> 00:26:43.520
Hello.
I'm Kim Jong-ki, it's good to meet you.

00:26:44.320 --> 00:26:44.640
Today,

00:26:44.920 --> 00:26:47.160
he is meeting a father of two children,

00:26:47.720 --> 00:26:50.880
whose 13-year-old daughter has just taken her own life.

00:26:53.760 --> 00:27:01.680
My poor man, I'm sorry for your loss.

00:27:09.360 --> 00:27:13.680
When I hear the sound of the wind,
I think of how my daughter

00:27:13.840 --> 00:27:17.760
must have felt when she jumped
from the 15th floor of our building.

00:27:19.200 --> 00:27:20.800
That is so sad.

00:27:26.400 --> 00:27:30.080
I have a lot of regrets.

00:27:33.920 --> 00:27:40.960
If I could have done something
when she was still alive,

00:27:41.120 --> 00:27:44.800
I wouldn't be so desperate and apathetic.

00:27:47.600 --> 00:27:53.440
After she died, I was angry,

00:27:56.240 --> 00:28:01.600
but now I don't even have that strength.

00:28:06.960 --> 00:28:13.360
I'm afraid to go any further.

00:28:13.840 --> 00:28:16.480
All I have left is my son...

00:28:18.880 --> 00:28:23.680
Isn't your first priority to take care of your family?

00:28:23.840 --> 00:28:25.120
Yes, it is.

00:28:25.280 --> 00:28:29.760
You must stand strong for them.
That's your role as a father.

00:28:29.920 --> 00:28:32.800
You are the backbone of your home.

00:28:36.040 --> 00:28:36.600
Every day,

00:28:37.080 --> 00:28:39.160
this father stands in front of the school,

00:28:39.720 --> 00:28:40.280
distraught.

00:28:41.600 --> 00:28:44.160
He's trying to understand what happened to his daughter,

00:28:44.960 --> 00:28:45.800
but he's all alone.

00:28:46.480 --> 00:28:48.600
He's left calling out to the pupils,

00:28:49.280 --> 00:28:53.160
trying to get from them the answers that the school won't give him.

00:28:56.000 --> 00:28:59.520
My daughter is dead! My daughter is dead!

00:28:59.680 --> 00:29:03.280
She sent you a message before she died!

00:29:10.240 --> 00:29:15.520
You were the last person she spoke to!
Tell me what happened!

00:29:15.680 --> 00:29:21.280
She jumped from the 15th floor!

00:29:36.880 --> 00:29:42.800
We take on a huge number of similar cases.

00:29:42.960 --> 00:29:46.720
These wounds are almost impossible to heal.

00:29:47.120 --> 00:29:51.680
More than individuals, it's the
whole family that breaks down.

00:29:51.840 --> 00:29:58.160
No one can cope alone,
and no one knows how to deal with it.

00:30:00.160 --> 00:30:08.160
And neither the school nor the
Ministry of Education will help them.

00:30:13.240 --> 00:30:16.040
He had planned some joint interventions at school

00:30:16.400 --> 00:30:17.880
along side Pyongyang Rim

00:30:18.520 --> 00:30:21.920
along side Pyongyang Rim

00:30:25.080 --> 00:30:26.600
The program is called Asago,

00:30:27.360 --> 00:30:28.040
the confession.

00:30:28.760 --> 00:30:31.360
It aims to get people talking about bullying.

00:30:36.760 --> 00:30:42.400
Pupils are called on to anonymously recount their experiences as bullies,

00:30:42.960 --> 00:30:45.600
as victims or just as witnesses.

00:30:51.920 --> 00:30:57.200
You know, my videos are shown
in a lot of schools, like this one,

00:30:57.360 --> 00:31:01.360
where I'm sometimes invited
to talk about school bullying.

00:31:01.520 --> 00:31:03.440
I'm "Mr Bullying.

00:31:06.080 --> 00:31:11.200
In fact, I had a beautiful son like all of you here,

00:31:11.360 --> 00:31:15.040
but I lost him because of bullying at school.

00:31:15.200 --> 00:31:19.760
I've decided to quit my job in
favour of this kind of activity,

00:31:19.920 --> 00:31:22.400
so that no one goes through the same thing.

00:31:24.720 --> 00:31:28.160
Hundreds of confessions are collected every term in this school.

00:31:28.720 --> 00:31:35.240
then explored in discussion groups to try and understand each other's feelings and experiences.

00:31:36.240 --> 00:31:42.560
I saw him push you and insult you.
I'm sorry I didn't say anything.

00:31:42.720 --> 00:31:46.000
I'm really sorry I didn't help you.

00:31:46.240 --> 00:31:51.760
I have a friend who has been bullied
since the beginning of the year.

00:31:51.920 --> 00:31:58.080
I feel guilty because I can't talk to him about
it for fear of how other people will look at me.

00:31:58.240 --> 00:32:03.440
A student might open up if you
talk to them, joke with them,

00:32:03.600 --> 00:32:07.280
have a laugh and have a good time together.

00:32:07.440 --> 00:32:13.840
Above all, you need to create an atmosphere
conducive to discussion and a relationship of trust.

00:32:14.000 --> 00:32:19.520
But that's hard to do, and that's why
most of them don't tell their parents.

00:32:19.680 --> 00:32:26.080
Does anyone here spend at least 5 hours
a week with their parents to talk or anything?

00:32:26.240 --> 00:32:28.480
That many people?

00:32:30.160 --> 00:32:34.400
My mum often asks me how things are at school.

00:32:34.560 --> 00:32:38.720
I answer her, but sometimes she
complains that I don't talk enough.

00:32:41.680 --> 00:32:48.000
Wouldn't it be nice if you could talk to your parents?

00:32:49.360 --> 00:32:57.040
Because if they know you well, they'll be able
to help or support you if you run into a problem.

00:32:57.200 --> 00:33:00.880
If you don't say anything, they won't know.

00:33:01.040 --> 00:33:08.800
My son never told me the truth either.
So I couldn't have known...

00:33:11.680 --> 00:33:15.040
Goodbye! Take care.

00:33:21.480 --> 00:33:22.800
When we met Pyo Ye Rim,

00:33:23.400 --> 00:33:25.360
we went back to see her old school.

00:33:26.480 --> 00:33:29.080
She hadn't been back there since she left school.

00:33:30.960 --> 00:33:38.640
It's overwhelming to realise what I've been through.

00:33:38.800 --> 00:33:46.720
When you look at that little school it's
hard to imagine how frightening it was.

00:33:46.880 --> 00:33:54.800
What kept me from running away and hiding?

00:33:59.520 --> 00:34:03.840
I wish I could have escaped.

00:34:04.080 --> 00:34:10.720
I regret not having been happy for so many years.

00:34:12.800 --> 00:34:16.960
I live with this disappointment.

00:34:18.400 --> 00:34:25.520
Now I have to learn to live with
these memories and move on.

00:34:29.840 --> 00:34:36.960
I need to be happy in my life.

00:34:40.040 --> 00:34:43.360
Pyo Ye Rim was never able to build a new life for herself.

00:34:44.160 --> 00:34:46.400
She used social media to fight her battle.

00:34:47.200 --> 00:34:52.440
But she received an outpouring of hateful messages on those same platforms.

00:34:53.280 --> 00:34:54.640
A never-ending cycle.

00:34:56.000 --> 00:34:59.440
We had planned one final shoot to finish the film.

00:35:06.640 --> 00:35:14.400
Mum, dad, I'm sorry, for everything until I die.

00:35:14.560 --> 00:35:17.520
It's all my fault.

00:35:21.040 --> 00:35:24.960
You told me that life had no meaning without me,

00:35:25.120 --> 00:35:28.880
but I'm not going to be able to listen to you.

00:35:29.440 --> 00:35:32.960
I can't begin to imagine your pain...

00:35:34.240 --> 00:35:38.480
the pain of seeing your child go first. I'm so sorry.

00:35:43.840 --> 00:35:50.640
I'm ashamed to admit it, even though I'm giving up,

00:35:51.520 --> 00:35:57.520
but I dare to hope that other
people won't give up my fight.

00:35:57.680 --> 00:36:02.960
My death may not mean much, but I beg you,

00:36:03.120 --> 00:36:10.880
at least let my petition be useful and let this
law be seriously considered until it is applied.

00:36:14.000 --> 00:36:16.000
I rely on you.

00:36:23.600 --> 00:36:25.440
One year after her death,

00:36:26.120 --> 00:36:28.040
There is no change in the situation.

00:36:28.760 --> 00:36:31.200
The bill has still not been passed.

00:36:33.520 --> 00:36:39.680
Acts of bullying at school are still subject to a three-year statute of limitations.

